        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "90fbcaa1-1280-56a9-a2fe-36e5fd7770c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: High Plains, Western High Plains, Trans-Pecos, West Texas, Western Rockies, Llano Estacado\n- Geological formations: Buda Limestone, Woodbine Formation, Maness Shale, Eagle Ford Group, Austin Chalk\n- Time periods: Late Cretaceous, Paleo-Indian, Archaic\n- Works: People of the Fire\n- Concepts: climatic warming, Native American cultural transition\n\nFacts:\n- The Buda Limestone is a geological formation in the High Plains and Trans-Pecos regions of West Texas, and its strata date to the Late Cretaceous.\n- The Woodbine Formation overlies the Maness Shale, the Buda Limestone, or older rocks.\n- The Woodbine Formation underlies the Eagle Ford Group or the Austin Chalk.\n- The southern part of the Western High Plains ecology region contains the geological formation called Llano Estacado, which is visible from a short distance or on satellite maps.\n- People of the Fire dramatizes a Native American cultural transition from the Paleo-Indian period to the Archaic period caused by climatic warming.\n- People of the Fire is set in the High Plains and Western Rockies region.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8717826b-de6c-5072-83ef-7c676c5584b2",
        "text": "Page: Buda Limestone. Sentence: The Buda Limestone is a geological formation in the High Plains and Trans-Pecos regions of West Texas whose strata date back to the Late Cretaceous.\nPage: High Plains (United States). Sentence: The southern region of the Western High Plains ecology region contains the geological formation known as Llano Estacado which can be seen from a short distance or from on satellite maps.\nPage: Woodbine Formation. Sentence: The Woodbine overlies the Maness Shale, Buda Limestone, or older rocks, and underlies the Eagle Ford Group or Austin Chalk.\nPage: People of the Fire. Sentence: It dramatizes the transition of Native American culture from Paleo-Indian to Archaic as a result of climatic warming, set in the High Plains and Western Rockies region.",
